{"id":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"Deferrals","desc":"NO DEFERRALS (the human, 2026-08-22): a PR ships everything its item names and everything it spots in touched code; what cannot be done STOPS and ASKS. The Inbox holds only what the human chooses to park. ONE exception: a test found flaky on master that a PR does not own is NOT a deferral — it goes to the Inbox's top-level `flaky tests` ledger, governed by dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY.","created":"2026-08-21T17:25:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:22:09-04:00"}
{"id":"flaky-tests","ord":"a7","title":"flaky tests — the ledger of tests found flaky on master that no PR owns","desc":"THE LEDGER, not the law: one entry per test file, sightings and dispositions as props on each entry. THE LAW lives in the boot chain — dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY (filed here, dispatched immediately, pi or grok never Opus, one PR when several are open, auto-merge on green). The CI-runs doorbell and the orchestrator's own reading of run logs are the reporting channel (the claude-ci watcher seat retired on the human's ban, 2026-09-01); the orchestrator files what they surface.","created":"2026-08-22T11:51:06-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T20:18:25-04:00"}
{"id":"awaiting-word","ord":"a8","title":"Awaiting the human's word","desc":"The orchestrator's surfaced-but-unruled ledger, per orch-findings-inbox: each child names a proposal or observation and the word it awaits. Ruled children get their outcome written and are trashed or promoted to a lane.","created":"2026-08-29T11:40:15-04:00"}
{"id":"design-decisions","ord":"a9","title":"design decisions — agents' judgment calls awaiting the human's review","desc":"Choices agents made on their own, for your review — ONLY two kinds reach this queue (your ruling, 2026-08-29 20:15): (1) decisions with USER-FACING impact (what you see, how it behaves, where your data/config lives); (2) creation or non-creation of packages/*. Everything lower-level stays in the PR body's ## Design decisions section for reviewers and never lands here. One parent per PR, one child per qualifying choice, plain words. Reviewed: fine → trash; wrong → a lane to reverse it.","created":"2026-08-29T17:29:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T20:17:08-04:00"}
{"id":"spaces-chat-write-scope","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a4","title":"Grant `chat:write` on the kolu Spaces app and reinstall it","done":"2026-09-03T09:15:03-04:00","desc":"Your live test of #460 (2026-09-02 ~12:37 ET): olai posted, Spaces refused it 403 `missing_permission` — the app JWT lacks `chat:write`. Grok's read: the fix is on the Spaces app, not in olai — grant the scope, reinstall so the grant is approved, and if the JWT is re-issued put it in `$OLAI_SPACES_TOKEN` and restart. The queue keeps the refused digest and retries once the token is accepted; the pill turns from `spaces fault` to `spaces` on the first success. The lane's merge waits on this test passing.","created":"2026-09-02T12:49:11-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T09:15:03-04:00","custom":{"node":"plugin-spaces-mirror","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/460"}}
{"id":"deferral-483-shutdown-unwind","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a2","title":"#483: shutdown does not unwind the plugin runtime","done":"2026-09-03T07:21:34-04:00","desc":"RESOLVED 2026-09-03: the third review round's SHOULD 3 showed shutdown already unwinds the plugins by construction (`Effect.scoped` around the command, provisions revoked, each revocation unloading the fibers that named it), with a bench pinning the one shape it misses (a plugin with an empty `needs`). Written into `openHost`'s doc in #483 (commit ff39126a). The human's approval of #483 covers it.","created":"2026-09-02T22:47:32-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T07:21:34-04:00","custom":{"node":"plugin-api-effect","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/483"}}
{"id":"await-morning-2026-09-03","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a6","title":"Morning digest 2026-09-03: what the night did, what awaits your word","done":"2026-09-03T09:14:07-04:00","desc":"CLOSED 2026-09-03 ~09:20 ET on the human's word (\"process away\"): everything it listed is settled — #480 merged overnight; #481, #482, #485 merged on the morning's rulings; #484 rejected and closed; #483 took the human's own review round and merged 07:21 ET as 31f85927. What it said, for history: MERGED overnight: #480 (one directory per plugin, 39m). GREEN AND PARKED on your word: #481 settle-from-the-run, #482 the Unassigned row in a fresh vault, #484 nags coalesce, #485 the missing chords, #483 the plugin API is Effect. Findings filed that night: the CI status plugin's 'ended without deciding' misfire on a just-born run (doorbell-undecided-at-start).","created":"2026-09-03T01:21:46-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T09:14:07-04:00","custom":{"node":"day-2026-09-02"}}
{"id":"deferral-486-npm-shim","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a3","title":"#486: the npm shim stays one lockfile, not one per engine plugin","done":"2026-09-03T09:12:46-04:00","desc":"APPROVED by the human 2026-09-03 ~09:15 ET, on the condition that it is documented — verified on the branch: `acp/README.md` gains a section \"Why one lockfile carries two adapters\", stating the reason and the cost (bumping either adapter moves the hash for both). The author's argument: one fixed-output derivation and one `npmDepsHash`; splitting would cost two large FODs and two hashes kept in step by hand for no separation the phase asked for.","created":"2026-09-03T09:04:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T09:12:46-04:00","custom":{"node":"agents-as-plugins","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/486"}}
{"id":"deferral-486-model-picker","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a4","title":"#486: the plan's \"Claude's model picker out of @olai/web\" clause has no subject","done":"2026-09-03T09:12:46-04:00","desc":"RULED by the human 2026-09-03 ~09:15 ET: the plan was wrong, not the PR — they asked Fable to correct brainstorming/cordis-for-olai.md. Nothing owed by #486. The author's finding: there is no model picker in the browser; the alias tiers moved into `olai-plugin-claude` on the server half, where the name is resolved; `fence.test.ts` proves `@olai/web` spells no engine.","created":"2026-09-03T09:04:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T09:12:46-04:00","custom":{"node":"agents-as-plugins","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/486"}}
{"id":"deferral-486-panel-e2e","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a5","title":"#486: no new e2e scenario for the plugins panel's engine rows","done":"2026-09-03T09:12:46-04:00","desc":"ACCEPTED by the human 2026-09-03 ~09:15 ET (\"fine/ignore\"): no follow-up filed. The panel had no e2e coverage before; the new reading is a unit case in `runtime.test.ts`.","created":"2026-09-03T09:04:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T09:12:46-04:00","custom":{"node":"agents-as-plugins","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/486"}}
{"id":"await-486-session-context","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a8","title":"#486's author session is at 97% of its 1M context before the refactor pass","done":"2026-09-03T09:09:26-04:00","desc":"Ruled 2026-09-03 ~09:10 ET: the human compacted the session themselves. The refactor pass proceeds in it.","created":"2026-09-03T09:04:55-04:00","changed":"2026-09-03T09:09:26-04:00","custom":{"node":"agents-as-plugins","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/486"}}
